<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns AA to NSW Treasury dual samurai bonds.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns AA to NSW Treasury dual samurai bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp said on Wednesday that it had assigned AA ratings to two yen/Australian dollar samurai bond issues by New South Wales Treasury Corp.</p>
<p>One issue is a 5.6 percent 10 billion yen samurai bond issue and the other a 3.8 percent 15 billion yen issue, both of which mature on October 25, 1999.</p>
<p>The ratings reflect that of the bonds' guarantor, the State of New South Wales, it said.</p>
<p>The rating is constrained by Australia's foreign currency sovereign rating of AA, it said, adding that the foreign currency rating outlook is positive.</p>
</text>
